			{Key: "←/esc", Description: "Back to the sessions"},
			{Key: "tab", Description: "Switch between the Agents and Breakdown tabs (inside a session)"},
			{Key: "/", Description: "Filter by project or session ID (not on Breakdown)"},
			{Key: ".", Description: "Cycle the sort column (agents: tree, Total largest first, Total smallest first; not on Breakdown)"},
			{Key: "↑↓/pgup/pgdn/home/end", Description: "Scroll the Breakdown tab"},
			{Key: "ctrl+p", Description: "Open command mode"},
			{Key: "?", Description: "Show this help"},
		},
		Sections: []help.Section{
			{
				Title: "Columns",
				Body: "Project: the working directory the session ran in, with your home folded to ~. " +
					"A long path is cut from the left so the project's own name stays visible; a dash means the transcript named none.\n" +
					"Last active: when the session's transcript was last written, in local time.\n" +
					"Session: the start of the session ID. The filter matches the full ID.",
			},
			{
				Title: "Where sessions come from",
				Body: "Claude Code keeps one transcript per session under projects/ in its configuration directory: " +
					"$CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR when set, otherwise ~/.claude. " +
					"Claude Code deletes old transcripts itself (after 30 days by default), so older sessions disappear from here too.\n" +
					"Sessions that could not be listed (symbolic links, which are refused rather than followed, unreadable directories, " +
					"or sessions beyond the listing cap) are counted as Skipped in the header.",
			},
			{
				Title: "Agents",
				Body: "Opening a session lists its agents: the orchestrator first, then each sub-agent with its type, " +
					"as a tree, with the models used and the tokens in, out, and cached.\n" +
					"The breadcrumb (Sessions › project › session ID) sits on the top border of the frame, not in the footer; " +
					"it is shortened on a narrow terminal and hidden when it no longer fits.\n" +
					"A ≥ before an Out count means a floor: that sub-agent's transcript was still being written, so the real figure is higher.\n" +
					"The orchestrator is the main conversation; its figures are never a floor.\n" +
					"When part of a transcript could not be read, the footer says the totals are approximate.",
			},
			{
				Title: "Agent columns",
				Body: "Agent: the orchestrator, or the sub-agent's type. ID: the start of the sub-agent's ID, long enough to tell two agents of the same type apart; " +
					"the orchestrator shows a dash. The filter matches the full ID.\n" +
					"State: running, idle, done or unknown. A sub-agent that finished is done. " +
					"One still running with no new transcript line for more than 5 min is idle. " +
					"The orchestrator is never done: it is running or idle while updates are live, and unknown once they pause. " +
					"A sub-agent whose state the files do not say is unknown once updates pause.\n" +
					"Tools: distinct tool calls read from the transcript.\n" +
					"Duration: first to last line of the transcript, wall clock, pauses included; a dash when the transcript has no timestamps.\n" +
					"Est. cost: the estimated cost in USD, see Costs. A sub-agent's is a floor (≥ ~) while its transcript may be incomplete; a dash means it cannot be computed.\n" +
					"Breakdown: how the agent's tokens split, in a bar of ten cells. Colors, left to right: Input, Output, Cache write, Cache read. " +
					"A category worth less than half a cell gets no cell of its own. The glyph follows app.gauge_glyph; a dash means no tokens.\n" +
					"Model, In, Out, Cache read, Cache write, Total: models used and token counts. " +
					"On a narrow terminal Cache write goes first, then Est. cost, Cache read, In, Breakdown, Model, State, Duration and Tools. Agent, ID, Out, Total and Share stay. " +
					"Cache write, Est. cost, Cache read, In and Breakdown give way before an agent's type is cut; Model, State, Duration and Tools do not.\n" +
					"Share: the agent's part of the session total, to one decimal, rounded down. " +
					"The orchestrator takes the rounding remainder, so the column adds up to 100%. A dash means the session has no tokens.\n" +
					"Press . to cycle: tree, then Total largest first, then Total smallest first, then the tree again. " +
					"Sorted, the list is flat: the branches go away. The sort stays when you open another session or press ctrl+r.",
			},
			{
				Title: "Breakdown",
				Body: "Press tab inside a session to switch between Agents and Breakdown; esc or ← leaves the session from either tab, and the next session opens on Agents.\n" +
					"The Breakdown tab splits the tokens of the whole session in three blocks, each with a Share and a Tokens column and a Total line: " +
					"by category (Input, Output, Cache write 5 min, Cache write 1 h, Cache read, with a swatch in the color the bar uses), by model, and by agent.\n" +
					"Share is the part of the session's tokens, to one decimal, never of the cost. The rounding remainder goes to the largest line so each block adds up to 100%. " +
					"A session with no tokens shows a dash for every share.\n" +
					"Tokens with no model name in the transcript are counted under unknown. The agent block matches the Share column of the Agents tab.\n" +
					"The panel ignores the filter and the sort: it always covers the whole session, and so do the Agents, Tokens and Est. cost in the header while it is on screen. " +
					"It updates live with the session. A panel taller than the screen scrolls with ↑↓, pgup, pgdn, home and end.",
			},
			{
				Title: "Costs",
				Body: "Est. cost is an estimate, marked ~: tokens times the prices you set, not a bill. DevDesk ships no price. " +
					"An agent whose model has no price shows a dash, never 0, and so does the header total. " +
					"A sub-agent's cost is a floor (≥ ~) because its transcript may be incomplete.\n" +
					"Billed is Claude Code's own total for the session, when it recorded one; a session still running has none. " +
					"Unattributed is Billed minus the estimates: what the estimate does not explain (web search is never priced). " +
					"A negative Unattributed, in orange, means your prices are higher than what was billed. " +
					"When there are no tokens in any agent, Unattributed is Billed (the whole bill). Est. cost follows the filter; Billed and Unattributed do not.\n" +
					"Set agent_usage.prices in the context's config file, in USD per million tokens, all five rates per model:\n" +
					"agent_usage:\n" +
					"  prices:\n" +
					"    claude-example-model:\n" +
					"      input: 3\n" +
					"      output: 15\n" +
					"      cache_write_5m: 3.75\n" +
					"      cache_write_1h: 6\n" +
					"      cache_read: 0.3\n" +
					"Model names match case-insensitively, with or without a trailing -YYYYMMDD date suffix. " +
					"Prices are read again on restart or when you change context; ctrl+r does not re-read them.",
			},
			{
				Title: "Live updates",
				Body: "While a session is open and still active, its figures are refreshed every 2 s and the header shows Updates: live.\n" +
					"Updates pause after 5 min without activity once every agent has finished (a session with an unfinished sub-agent stays live), or when its transcript is deleted: the header shows Updates: paused.\n" +
					"An agent still running with no new transcript line for more than 5 min is shown idle; a long tool call does that too. The header counts the idle agents.\n" +
					"Press ctrl+r to resume. Re-read the whole session from the start with ctrl+r; coming back to the view only reads what changed since the last point read, and goes back to live if the session is being written to.\n" +
